<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Telaga Batu inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Telaga Batu inscription is a large stone found at Telaga Batu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, inscribed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-malay">Old Malay</a> in the late seventh century during the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> period. Crowned by seven cobra heads and with a spout for water, it carries a long oath of loyalty with curses against officials and subjects who betray the king, and lists many ranks, from princes and governors to scribes and merchants, giving a rare picture of Srivijayan government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/telaga-batu-inscription.jpg" alt="Telaga Batu inscription" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Telaga_Batu_inscription.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
